{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbTH3yotB7kAVcsXxCLs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, `asymmetric_ideal_alternation_mirror`, and the self-check passed (`OK`). It refines the incumbent `individual_alternation_sensitivity_mirror`.\n\n**The one change:** the incumbent penalises any departure from a person's ideal switching rate the same way in both directions. In this version, switching *more* often than one's ideal costs a shared fraction (`omega`) of what switching *less* often costs. `omega`'s prior is centred on 1, so the data decide whether people go easier on over-alternation. Everything else is kept as it was: each person's ideal rate and sensitivity, their weights on heads/tails imbalance and the longest streak, the shared weights on the final streak and on palindromes, and the personal guessing rate.\n\n**Why this change:** it targets the critique's strongest discrepancy, which survives the FDR correction (z=3.89, q=0.016). When both sequences alternate a lot, people pick the more alternating one 59% of the time, but the incumbent predicts 48%. A same-sized penalty either side of the ideal can't produce that gap.\n\n**Self-check results:**\n- It passed the import allowlist, the finite log-probability check and the data contract.\n- The short smoke fit (100 draws, 1 chain) gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −2295.7. That's slightly better than the incumbent's −2301.4, but a single short chain can't be compared fairly with a full fit.\n- The check also warned that PSIS-LOO looked unreliable: 8% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5. I didn't follow this up. I'd guess it comes from the very short fit, but if it holds in admission's full fit, this model's ELPD would be flagged as untrustworthy.\n- Not checked here: novelty against the live models, convergence and the 30-minute speed limit. Admission's full fit decides those.\n\nFiles are in `.../experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4489,"cache_read_input_tokens":78184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4489,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d68c4317-994e-4209-95c4-5e644100e71a","uuid":"4749e084-c382-49d9-83a3-8d4063279b18","timestamp":"2026-10-01T11:40:22.077Z","request_id":"req_011CfbTH3WnZi5qfL6RiucZ9"}
